  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) achieved 0.591 acc, a large jump over config_001 (singleprofile, 0.485), confirming that multiprofile aggregation is the most impactful design choice so far. Image-only (config_010) is very weak (0.208), so RNA is the dominant signal. Uncertainty: we do not yet know whether transformer aggregation outperforms simple avgpool for combining multiple profiles—this is the key mechanism enabling the multiprofile gain. This experiment (config_003) isolates exactly one variable (aggregation: transformer vs avgpool) while holding RNA encoder (pca_n2000) and profile setting (multiprofile) constant, giving a clean comparison against config_002. If transformer substantially exceeds avgpool, it tells us the aggregation architecture is a high-leverage knob to exploit in later multimodal experiments; if not, avgpool is sufficient and we can redirect budget toward encoder or fusion choices. Under a tight budget, this single-variable test on the strongest-performing branch is the most information-efficient next step."
}

